  "id": "Compound::DB01026 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Ketoconazole is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2b6 through a multi-step mechanism involving the cytochrome P450 system. The evidence suggests that Ketoconazole, through its inclusion in the Cytochrome P450 3a4 Inhibitors class, indirectly influences Cyp2b6 via Ritonavir, which binds to Cyp2b6. This pathway is supported by the observed binding of Ketoconazole to Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p, which in turn is bound by Ritonavir, ultimately leading to the inhibition of Cyp2b6. The shared lowest common ancestors, such as Ketoconazole and Ritonavir, highlight the interconnectedness of these entities within the context of anti-infective and azole-related pathways. The integration of these relationships underscores the role of Ketoconazole in modulating Cyp2b6 through its interaction with Ritonavir, suggesting a potential regulatory mechanism that is both contextually and mechanistically relevant.",
